{'symbol': 'PCG', 'date': '2020-07-01 20:30:00', 'title': 'PG&E EMERGES FROM CHAPTER 11', 'text': 'PG&E EMERGES FROM CHAPTER 11.PG&E CORP - PG&E OBTAINS ALL FINANCING NECESSARY TO EMERGE FROM CHAPTER 11 AND FOR ONGOING OPERATIONS.PG&E CORP - FUNDS FIRE VICTIM TRUST WITH $5.4 BILLION IN CASH AND COMMON STOCK REPRESENTING 22.19% OWNERSHIP STAKE IN PG&E CORPORATION.PG&E CORP - HAS SEATED ITS NEW BOARD OF DIRECTORS.PG&E CORP - PG&E TODAY DEPOSITED APPROXIMATELY $5 BILLION IN WILDFIRE FUND.PG&E CORP - NEW BOARD CONSISTS OF 14 MEMBERS, 11 OF WHOM ARE NEW.PG&E CORP - FIRE VICTIM TRUST FUNDING SCHEDULE CONSISTS OF $5.4 BILLION IN CASH ON PLAN EFFECTIVE DATE, WHICH WAS JULY 1, 2020.PG&E CORP - FIRE VICTIM TRUST FUNDING SCHEDULE CONSISTS OF ADDITIONAL $1.35 BILLION IN CASH IN TWO INSTALLMENTS IN 2021 AND 2022.PG&E CORP - IN ADDITION TO FUNDING FIRE VICTIM TRUST, PG&E HAS ALSO NOW FUNDED TWO ADDITIONAL WILDFIRE SETTLEMENTS.PG&E CORP - ON JULY 1, 2020, PG&E IMPLEMENTED NOTEHOLDER RESTRUCTURING SUPPORT AGREEMENT.'}